    "semantics": "Exact for this fixed model and the selected provenance-group withdrawal space. Withdrawing a group removes every recorded BINDS edge mentioning that provider label or imported PubMed identifier, including records with other annotations. Overlapping groups remove a record once. An annotation is not proof of independent corroboration, and a PubMed group is not necessarily one experiment. This is a conservative record-quarantine stress scenario, not a factual retraction, clinical effect, or probability of error. All competing compounds change jointly. Protected groups are assumed unavailable for withdrawal; protection does not mean a review or experiment has established that assumption. Binary64 exactness is relative to the declared scorer and numerical runtime; verification rejects numerical mismatches. Other relation families, new records, refitting and unselected groups are outside scope."
  },
